WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.800
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:12.240
AI research is improving at such a rapid pace,&nbsp;
that today, we can not only create virtual humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:18.320
but, even exert some artistic control&nbsp;
over how these virtual humans should look.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:26.080
But today, we can do something even cooler.&nbsp;
What can be even cooler than that? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:31.600
have you ever seen someone with a really cool&nbsp;
haircut and wondered what you would like with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:38.880
it? Would it be ridiculous? Or would you be able&nbsp;
to pull it off? Well, hold on to your papers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:44.880
because you don’t have to wonder anymore. With&nbsp;
this new AI, you can visualize that yourself!

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:52.800
Hmm, okay, but wait a second. Previous&nbsp;
methods were already able to do that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.800 --> 00:01:00.880
so, what is new here? Well, yes! But look at&nbsp;
the quality of the results. In some cases, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:08.560
is quite easy to find out that these are synthetic&nbsp;
images, while for other cases, so many of the fine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:14.320
details of the face get lost in the process&nbsp;
that the end result is not that convincing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:21.360
So, is that it? Is the hairstyle synthesis&nbsp;
dream dead? Well, if you have been holding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:29.200
on to your papers, now squeeze that paper, and&nbsp;
have a look at this new technique. And, wow!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.800
My goodness, just look at that. This is a huge&nbsp;
improvement just one more paper down the line.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.920
And note that these previous methods&nbsp;
were not some ancient techniques,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:52.080
these are from just one and two years ago. So&nbsp;
much improvement in so little time. I love it.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:59.200
Now let’s see what more it can do. Look… we&nbsp;
can choose the hairstyle we are looking for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:07.520
and, yes! It doesn’t just give us just one image&nbsp;
to work with, no! It gradually morphs our hair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:15.040
into the desired target shape. That is fantastic,&nbsp;
because even if we don’t like the final hairstyle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:21.280
one of these intermediate images may give&nbsp;
us just what we are looking for. Loving it.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:29.280
And it has one more fantastic property. Look. Most&nbsp;
of the details of the face remain in the final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:35.840
results. Phew! We don’t even have to morph into&nbsp;
a different person to be able to pull this off.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.520
Now, interestingly, look,&nbsp;
the eye color may change,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:48.000
but the rest seems to be very close to&nbsp;
the original. Not perfect, but very close.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:56.640
And, did you notice? Yes, it gets better!&nbsp;
Way better! We can even choose the structure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:00.240
this would be the hairstyle,&nbsp;
which can be one image,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:07.600
and the appearance, this is more like the&nbsp;
hair color. So, does that mean that? Yes!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:15.440
We can even choose them separately. That is,&nbsp;
take two hairstyles, and fuse them together.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:22.560
Now, have a look at this too. This one is an&nbsp;
exclusive example, to the best of my knowledge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:28.080
you can only see this here on Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers. A huge thank you for the authors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:35.440
for creating these just for us. And I must&nbsp;
say that we could stop on any of these images,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:42.080
and I am not sure if I would be able to tell&nbsp;
that it is synthetic. I may have a hunch due&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:48.800
to how flamboyant some of these hairstyles are,&nbsp;
but not due to quality concerns, that’s for sure.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:53.200
Even if we subject these&nbsp;
images to closer inspection,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:58.160
the visual artifacts of the previous&nbsp;
techniques around the boundaries of the hair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:05.040
seem to be completely gone. And I wonder&nbsp;
what this will be able to do just a couple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:10.720
more papers down the line. What do you think? I’d&nbsp;
love to know, let me know in the comments below!

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:12.080
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

